# The shellcheck this project lints with, in one place, read by BOTH the CI
# workflow and the local prek hook. They used to differ: CI took whatever
# shipped on the runner image while the hook used whatever was installed
# locally, and the two reported the same construct differently. A disable
# written against one of them was green locally and red in CI, and a branch was
# pushed on the strength of the local run.
#
# The two codes are NOT the same check. SC2317 flags a STATEMENT it believes
# cannot be reached, and fires on genuinely dead code as well. SC2329 flags a
# FUNCTION DEFINITION that is never invoked. They overlap only here: 0.11
# introduced SC2329 and narrowed SC2317 so it no longer reports every line
# inside an uncalled function, where older builds did. So the version decides
# which one you get, and SC2329 is the narrower disable -- suppressing SC2317
# in that scope would also hide real unreachable code.
#
# Sourced as shell, so it stays readable from both.
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.11.0
# sha256 of shellcheck-v${SHELLCHECK_VERSION}.linux.x86_64.tar.xz, from the
# release. Verified before use; a download nobody checks is a dependency that
# can change under you.
SHELLCHECK_SHA256_LINUX_X86_64=8c3be12b05d5c177a04c29e3c78ce89ac86f1595681cab149b65b97c4e227198
